    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Rules of the N-Deklination",
     "texto": [
      "This group includes masculine nouns that refer to people or animals:",
      "1. Nouns ending in **-e**: **der Kollege, der Kunde, der Zeuge, der Experte, der Löwe** (acc./dat./gen.: **den/dem/des Kollegen, Kunden, Zeugen**).",
      "2. Nouns of Greek or Latin origin ending in stressed suffixes such as **-ant, -ent, -ist, -at**: **der Praktikant, der Assistent, der Polizist, der Diplomat** (acc./dat./gen.: **-en**).",
      "3. Notable exceptions: **der Herr** (oblique singular: **Herrn**; plural: **Herren**), **der Nachbar** (oblique: **Nachbarn**). In the genitive they do not add «-s» but keep the ending «-(e)n»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
